WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.163 --> 00:00:01.985
(energetic music)

00:00:01.985 --> 00:00:03.548
- First came the grasses.

00:00:03.548 --> 00:00:05.131
They came in thick.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.917
Then smaller shrubs.

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:12.928
With them, the insects returned.

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:15.622
Then the trees, and with the trees,

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:17.789
the monkeys and elephants.

00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:23.803
Here at Sai Sanctuary, we
have over 300 acres of forest

00:00:25.923 --> 00:00:29.923
that we have replanted
and brought back to life.

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:39.026
My full name is Pamela Gale Malhotra,

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:43.193
and I'm co-founder, with my
husband, of Sai Sanctuary Trust.

00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:48.601
It had always been our dream

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:52.601
to have a private forest
sanctuary for wildlife,

00:00:54.556 --> 00:00:57.744
where they would be protected.

00:00:57.744 --> 00:00:59.979
When we first came here,

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:02.334
most of the lands that were sold to us,

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.220
were abandoned lands.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.947
Abandoned rice fields, coffee,
and cardamom fields as well.

00:01:08.947 --> 00:01:12.197
A lot of deforestation had taken place.

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:15.897
And that took a lot,
a lot of care and energy

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:19.027
and time and years to bring it back.

00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:20.544
- She'd really done well this year.

00:01:20.544 --> 00:01:21.996
- Yeah, they seem really well.

00:01:21.996 --> 00:01:24.908
People thought we were quite
crazy, but that's okay.

00:01:24.908 --> 00:01:26.250
A lot of people have thought

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.417
people that have done some
amazing things were crazy.

00:01:31.254 --> 00:01:33.970
(playful music)

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:37.333
(camera clicks)

00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:41.500
Here in the sanctuary, it
is a biodiversity hotspot.

00:01:43.419 --> 00:01:45.486
I remember walking through the forest,

00:01:45.486 --> 00:01:50.115
you wouldn't hear anything but
the sound of your own feet.

00:01:50.115 --> 00:01:53.448
Now, the place is alive with sound.

00:01:53.448 --> 00:01:57.115
(birds cawing and chirping)

00:01:57.958 --> 00:02:01.708
One of our main sound
makers are the cicadas.

00:02:03.554 --> 00:02:07.721
They have a tremendous
decibel range (laughs).

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.506
Here they start again.

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.099
(cicadas buzzing)

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.194
We keep striving to do more and more,

00:02:16.194 --> 00:02:20.277
but the initial goal has
been more than achieved.

00:02:21.268 --> 00:02:25.134
My hope for the next 10
years for this forest

00:02:25.134 --> 00:02:29.301
is that it will continue to
be protected and expanded.

00:02:31.812 --> 00:02:35.454
We both feel a tremendous amount of joy

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.930
when we walk through the sanctuary.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.922
I've never felt this kind of joy

00:02:40.922 --> 00:02:44.505
in anything else that
I've done in my life.

